+/// Whether the kernel can handle IPv6 at all.
+///
+/// This is not the same as IPv6 being enabled: `/proc/sys/net/ipv6` exists whenever the kernel
+/// has IPv6, also when it is disabled with the `disable_ipv6` sysctl. It is missing when the
+/// kernel is built without IPv6 (`CONFIG_IPV6=n`), where nftables has neither the `inet` nor the
+/// `ip6` family, or when IPv6 is disabled at boot (`ipv6.disable=1`). In both cases the kernel
+/// handles no IPv6 traffic, so an `ip` table is enough.
+fn kernel_supports_ipv6() -> bool {
+    Path::new("/proc/sys/net/ipv6").exists()
+}
